{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll 3 tests pass. The SQLAlchemy 2.x modernization is complete.\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**`app/repository.py`**:\n- Replaced `session.query()` with SQLAlchemy 2.x `select()` statements\n- Removed implicit `commit()` from `create_entry()` - caller now controls transaction boundaries\n\n**`app/api.py`**:\n- Simplified - relies on caller for transaction management (no internal commits)\n\n**`app/worker.py`**:\n- Uses `flush()` for intermediate state persistence within a single transaction\n- Single `commit()` at the end; exceptions trigger automatic rollback\n\n**`app/admin_cli.py`**:\n- `plan_batch(dry_run=True): Explicitly restores original status and calls `rollback()`\n- `reconcile_batch(dry_run=True)`: Rolls back all changes at the end\n\n**`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`**:\n- Updated to document the new transaction boundary semantics"}}
